      ":question/id": "89e5f470-c1b5-55ea-b3e2-011a14a10a79",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are identity matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $M$ is *not* an identity matrix. It is diagonal, but its diagonal entries are not all ones: ${m}_{11}=3\\ne 1$.\n\n- $N$ is *not* an identity matrix. It is diagonal, but its diagonal entries are not all ones: ${n}_{22}=2\\ne 1$.\n\n- $P$ is an identity matrix. It is square, every main diagonal entry is one, and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\nTherefore, only $P$ is an identity matrix.",
