      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are identity matrices?\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$M=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$N=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n<div>$P=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nSelect all that apply.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "- $M$ is *not* an identity matrix. It is not a square matrix: it has 2 rows and 4 columns.\n\n- $N$ is an identity matrix. It is square, every main diagonal entry is one, and every off-diagonal entry is zero.\n\n- $P$ is *not* an identity matrix. It is square, but an entry off the main diagonal is nonzero: ${p}_{24}=-1\\ne 0$.\n\nTherefore, only $N$ is an identity matrix.",
